on the eve of 9 11 the biden  administration getting blasted for  working in tandem with the taliban the  same terror group that 20 years ago gave  safe harbor to al-qaeda the white house  even praising them as the professional  and business-like while 100 americans  are still stuck in afghanistan meanwhile  while white house press secretary jensen  saying today this about accountability  i'm curious if there have been any  offers of resignation from anyone in the  chain of command or  any anyone involved in the decisions  with the uh evacuation no  um so the president still has confidence  in those  yes  so  dana we are seeing this break between  generals leadership in the pentagon and  veterans of the afghanistan war in the  past couple of weeks as people try to  process how this happened to end this  way well it's interesting also just that  if if somebody has  something of yours that is of value and  you need to get it back but they hold  all the cards you're going to have to be  nice to them  until you get it back and  it could be that one of the reasons they  have to use words like businesslike and  is because  they want to make sure that they can get  the americans or green card holders or  the people who helped us in the war out  which is probably obviously not  happening you've seen some of the  pictures today we know what the taliban  is doing i've actually also in touch as  i know a lot of you are with some of  these groups private groups former  veterans and and others that are trying  to get people out and the taliban is  hunting them and and they know that and  so it's like they're one step ahead of  the taliban to try to get this done but  they also are holding their fire because  they need the cooperation of the state  department in order to help them now  this you pay a price for not having  anybody on the ground it's one of the  things that they keep saying at the um  state department and at the white house  is that well we don't have anyone on the  ground so we're trying our best and i  just think  is such a debacle i cannot believe that  that were that has happened and um you  know i was just you know we on newsroom  we had the interview with the  interpreter carl  and we keep track of his progress i mean  he is safe but  there's just very little that can be  done outside of these outside groups  yeah so jesse if you look at a 911  tomorrow in the situation that the  united states is in with very little  leverage if any over the taliban  you have people looking back on the past  20 years looking back at the actions of  the obama administration the fact that  some of the people they swapped for beau  bergdahl  are now back in charge we were told by  the by administration that they would  not make it back to the battlefield  let's take a look at what jens hockey  said about it in 2015 and get you to  react  was it worth it absolutely we have a  commitment to our men and women serving  oversea or serving in our military  defending our national security every  day that we're going to do everything to  bring them home if we can and that's  what we did in this case  jesse look at the lengths that we went  to to bring back a deserter  we did not go to those same lengths to  bring back  allies americans stranded americans and  it cost us lives marines are dead  because of it  tomorrow 9 11 the 20th anniversary was  supposed to be a major deal for the  biden presidency if you think about his  running mate launch that strike to kill  osama bin laden joe biden was supposed  to come in tomorrow and close the  chapter in an iconic way on america's  longest war  and he's not going to do that he's not  even going to speak tomorrow katie  because what is he supposed to say he  blew it so badly stranding americans we  lost people we shouldn't have lost we  armed the enemy and so now he's just  going to go through ceremonies what  would he say anyway katie would it be  well received  by the crowd i don't think so could he  come up with the right words live in the  moment to convey what he thought about  it i don't think he'd be able to pull it  off someone said he's going to keep his  mouth shut the commander-in-chief after  we ended 20 years of war so when you  hear about this heaping praise on the  taliban i get it dana's right it's a  delicate dance you have hostages there  so you got to play nice but it leaves a  disgusting taste in the mouth of  everybody that hears it because  the taliban  put bullets through gi's chests  shot limbs off of americans i have  pictures on my phone  afghan allies right now  whips on their back brutality like you  wouldn't believe so the reason we're  doing this is strategic but we're here  because biden's dumb decisions  he got us into this situation where we  have to heat praise and he'll have to  own that for the rest of you yeah  this is a you know people are trying to  act like in the administration that this  just happened that you know there was no  way to really plan for this but at the  same time we planned for every single  contingency but jesse's right there  everything that has happened with the  last month with afghanistan  was a result of decisions that were made  either by the administration recently or  in in years past and it's not just about  the 20th anniversary of 9 11 tomorrow  where as americans we should be  remembering what happened that day the  taliban is expected to announce their  government they are back in charge  they're going to embarrass us on 9 11  and yet they're saying oh they're very  business-like and we can work with them  i think it was a bizarre idea to want  peace by 9 11 and to work so hard to  bring it about so that  instead of grieving over the 20 years  and the the event itself the trauma that  scarred so many people we're talking  about the taliban whether or not they're  going to keep their deal and we're you  know we're totally totally distracted a  couple of quick points number one there  was a second 